//
// Why a new grant was needed. LICENSE.EXCEPTION carries two §7 permissions:
// Exception A covers compiler OUTPUT, Exception B covers designated runtime
// files linked into a program. Neither reaches compiler-INPUT source such as
// this. So this is a third, narrower carve-out — an exception to the exception —
// scoped exactly to the files in this directory.
//
// It changes nothing upstream: the Exsecutor original remains GPL-3.0-or-later,
// and no other Exsecutor source is relicensed by implication. See LICENSING.md
// and Documentation/DCF_EXSECUTOR.md.
//
// This file holds the `DeModFrame` declaration that the codec is certified
// against; upstream it is the §14 entry-23 fixture. Its original header follows.
//
// §14 entry 23 -- `DeModFrame` encode/decode against ALL 246 vectors of
// `vendor/hydramesh-wire/golden_vectors.json` -- byte-identical to every
// one of them. DIFFERENT IN KIND from every other entry (§14 says so
// itself): the other 23 are cases this project wrote for itself; this one
// is an EXTERNAL CERTIFICATE this project must satisfy. Under the
// certificate's own theorem (`vendor/hydramesh-wire/golden_vectors.json`'s
// "theorem" field, confirmed by reading the file directly: encode is
// affine over GF(2)^108 -> GF(2)^136 and the validity syndrome is affine
// GF(2)^136 -> GF(2)^16), matching all 246 vectors -- 109 in
// `encode_basis`, 137 in `syndrome_basis`, confirmed by counting the file's
// own arrays, not assumed from the "246" figure alone -- is equivalent to
// agreeing with the reference implementation on all 2^108 frames GIVEN
// THAT THE CODEC IS AFFINE (bit placement plus a CRC). That premise is
// argued from reading entry23/codex.exsc (docs/design/wire-codec.md
// section 5), not measured; the example frame in the stream's third
// section is one non-basis spot check of it, not a proof.
//
// §5.2's own worked example, verbatim:
//
//   @transitus
//   publica structura DeModFrame {
//       signum:  u8               // 0xD3, the first validity gate
//       versio:  u4               // packs MSB-first with genus
//       genus:   u4               // frame type
//       numerus: u16:maior
//       fons:    u16:maior
//       meta:    u16:maior
//       onus:    u32:maior
//       tempus:  u24:maior        // 24-bit microsecond offset
//       cursus:  u16:maior        // CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE over bytes 0..14
//   }
//
// This is the SAME declaration §5.2 attributes to `prototypes/wire/`
// checking its reading of the format against the same 246 vectors before
// attempting it. `prototypes/README.md` is explicit that nothing under
// `prototypes/` may become a build or test dependency ("Never shipped.
// Never on the build closure... may be referenced from Makefile, the Nix
// build, or compiler/, or otherwise become a build or test dependency"),
// so `prototypes/wire/wire_probe.py` is read for context ONLY (it is a
// design probe, not this suite's reference) and is never invoked from
// run_conformance_tests.
//
// RUN. The codec is written in Exsecutor: entry23/codex.exsc (pure -- no
// `poscit`, no `initium`) and entry23/probatio.exsc (the `initium` driver,
// the only file naming `Mundus`), compiled as ONE unit with this file first,
// so the declaration being certified is the one below, §5.2's verbatim.
// tests/run.sh's cert branch (cert_entry23) compiles, assembles and runs the
// unit, audits the binary (`write` and `exit_group` only), and compares the
// 2,502-byte stream it writes, section by section, with what
// entry23/expecta.py builds from the vendored JSON: sections 1-2 are the
// 246 certificate vectors, 3 the anchors, 4-5 the laws
// (docs/design/wire-codec.md section 6). Then three mechanical mutants --
// polynomial 0x1021 -> 0x1020, `numerus: u16:minor`, `versio`/`genus`
// swapped -- must each fail at the vector section 6.1 names. The mutants of
// this declaration are applied to a COPY of this file; the two lines they
// match (`    numerus: u16:maior`, and `versio`/`genus` adjacent) are
// load-bearing for the harness, which fails loudly if either moves.

@transitus
publica structura DeModFrame {
    signum:  u8
    versio:  u4
    genus:   u4
    numerus: u16:maior
    fons:    u16:maior
    meta:    u16:maior
    onus:    u32:maior
    tempus:  u24:maior
    cursus:  u16:maior
}

// TEST: entry=23 shape=cert status=run sources=entry23/codex.exsc,entry23/probatio.exsc
